    "title": "Giraffe at Gulf Breeze Zoo to make Super Bowl, weather predictions - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Richard Kim ,\n1 hours ago\nVideo above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Jan. 28, 2026\nGULF BREEZE, Fla. ( WKRG ) — A local zoo is set to hold its annual event to honor one of its four-legged residents.\nBlack bear spotted in Saraland According to a news release, the Gulf Breeze Zoo is holding its Third Annual Kenya Day at 9:30 a.m. on Monday, Feb. 2.\nInstead of the traditional Groundhog Day, the zoo takes the day to honor Kenya, a reticulated giraffe. Kenya will make two predictions: whether there will be six more weeks of winter or an early spring, and whether the Seattle Seahawks or the New England Patriots will win Super Bowl LX, which will be played on Sunday, Feb. 8, in San Francisco.\nKatelyn Peters, who serves as Guest Services Manager for the zoo, praised Kenya’s “big personality and playful energy,” saying that he had become a fan favorite amongst guests.\nVisitors this year can watch Kenya in action at the giraffe exhibit with apid admission to the zoo. Those opting to stay home can still see the predictions via a Facebook livestream.\nGulf Breeze Zoo cares for over 800 exotic animals. Many of these species are threatened and endangered, including the reticulated giraffe.\nPensacola scores two new Breeze Airways routes to ramp up summer service Those interested in learning more can visit https://www.gbzoo.com/events or call 866-620-1825.\nCopyright 2026 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to WKRG News 5.",
    "summary": "Video above: ‘News 5 Now’ — Top Stories from Jan. 28, 2026 GULF BREEZE, Fla. ( WKRG ) — A local zoo is set to hold its annual event to honor one of its four-legged residents. Black bear spotted in Saraland According to a news release, the Gulf Breeze Zoo is holding its Third Annual Kenya Day at 9:30 a.m. on Monday, Feb. 2.",
